 "requested_at": "2026-11-11T15:59:03.638871Z",
 "text": "The clause is not enforceable. It removes the written-notice requirement for showing a unit to prospective tenants, and the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 requires written notice for that kind of entry. Section 4 of the Act makes any term that contradicts the Act's protections void, so the landlord cannot rely on the clause to dispense with written notice. The oral or \"reasonable effort\" notice the clause substitutes does not satisfy the statute. The 8 a.m. to 8 p.m. window is consistent with the Act, but the notice term is not.\n\nI'm working from memory of the Act's structure, so please verify the exact wording of the entry provisions (in particular, which section sets out the written-notice requirement for showing units) against the current consolidation on e-Laws before relying on this.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 26",
